From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (agent session)" <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:05:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] renderer/d3d11: port the image (kitty graphics) pipeline to
 HLSL

Adds image.hlsl and wires the pipeline, leaving bg_image as the only one still
without shaders.

The image step passes a texture but NO sampler - the other backends rely on a
default existing in their pipeline state - so Pipeline carries one, borrowed
from Shaders, and RenderPass.step binds it when the step supplies none.
Without it the shader samples through a null sampler and reads black.

One real difference from the GLSL, found by the test rather than by reading:
the GLSL passes z = 1.0 into the projection, and ortho2d's z row is
{0, 0, -1, 0}, so z_clip becomes -1. OpenGL's NDC depth range is [-1, 1] where
that is just the near plane; D3D's is [0, 1], so the entire quad was clipped
and nothing drew. z is 0 here. I had originally copied the 1.0 across with a
comment claiming it kept the backends clipping alike, which was exactly
backwards.

The test renders a placement offscreen and asserts both that the inside is
opaque white AND that a pixel outside the destination rect is untouched. The
second half is what makes it a test of the *rect* rather than of something
having been drawn at all - the source_rect to texture-coordinate mapping and
the projection both have to be right to pass.

  default: 3086 pass, 58 skip, 0 fail

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
